# Spring Boot Best Practices

## Project Structure (Domain-Driven Design)

```
src/main/java/com/example/
├── {domain}/                    # One package per domain
│   ├── domain/                  # Domain layer - entities and repository interfaces
│   │   ├── {Entity}.java        # JPA entity
│   │   └── {Entity}Repository.java  # Spring Data JPA repository interface
│   ├── application/             # Application layer - business logic
│   │   └── {Entity}ApplicationService.java
│   └── interfaces/              # Interface layer - REST controllers
│       └── rest/
│           ├── {Entity}Controller.java
│           └── {Entity}Mapper.java
├── shared/                      # Cross-cutting concerns
│   ├── application/
│   ├── domain/
│   └── interfaces/rest/
└── api/generated/               # OpenAPI generated code (do not edit)
```

## Transaction Management

### Use @Transactional for Simplicity
Prefer the declarative `@Transactional` annotation for most use cases. It automatically wraps the entire method in a transaction, which is sufficient for typical operations.

```java
// Good - simple and clear
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ProjectApplicationService {
    private final ProjectRepository projectRepository;

    @Transactional
    public ProjectDto updateProject(String ref, UpdateProjectRequestDto request) {
        Project project = projectRepository.findByRef(ref)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new EntityNotFoundException("Project", ref));

        if (request.getTitle() != null) {
            project.setTitle(request.getTitle());
        }
        // ... other field updates

        return entityMapper.toDto(projectRepository.save(project));
    }
}
```

### When Minimal Transaction Scope Is Needed
For operations where the read operation is expensive and should not be part of the transaction, you can manually separate the read:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ProjectApplicationService {
    private final TransactionTemplate transactionTemplate;
    private final ProjectRepository projectRepository;
    private final EntityMapper entityMapper;

    public ProjectDto updateProjectWithMinimalTransaction(String ref, UpdateProjectRequestDto request) {
        Project project = projectRepository.findByRef(ref)  // Read outside transaction
            .orElseThrow(() -> new EntityNotFoundException("Project", ref));

        // Apply changes outside transaction
        if (request.getTitle() != null) {
            project.setTitle(request.getTitle());
        }

        // Only save inside transaction
        Project saved = transactionTemplate.execute(status -> projectRepository.save(project));
        return entityMapper.toDto(saved);
    }
}
```

### Full Transaction for Atomic Operations
When multiple writes must be atomic, use `@Transactional` or wrap the whole operation in `TransactionTemplate`:

```java
// Create needs full transaction for consistency
@Transactional
public ProjectDto createProject(CreateProjectRequestDto request) {
    int sequenceNumber = generateSequenceNumber();  // Part of transaction
    Project project = new Project(request.getTitle(), sequenceNumber);
    return entityMapper.toDto(projectRepository.save(project));
}
```

## Lombok Usage

### Use @RequiredArgsConstructor for Dependency Injection

```java
// Good
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ProjectApplicationService {
    private final ProjectRepository projectRepository;
    private final EntityMapper entityMapper;
}
```

### Standard Lombok Annotations for Entities

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "projects")
@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor(access = AccessLevel.PROTECTED)
public class Project {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long projectId;

    private String title;
    private int sequenceNumber;

    public Project(String title, int sequenceNumber) {
        this.title = title;
        this.sequenceNumber = sequenceNumber;
    }
}
```

## OpenAPI Generated Code

### DTO Suffix Convention
All generated model classes use `Dto` suffix:

- Domain: `Project`
- DTOs: `ProjectDto`, `CreateProjectRequestDto`, `UpdateProjectRequestDto`

### Controller Implementation
Controllers implement generated API interfaces:

```java
@RestController
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ProjectController implements ProjectsApi {
    private final ProjectApplicationService projectApplicationService;

    @Override
    public ResponseEntity<ProjectDto> createProject(CreateProjectRequestDto request) {
        ProjectDto created = projectApplicationService.createProject(request);
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(created);
    }

    @Override
    public ResponseEntity<ProjectDto> getProjectByRef(String ref) {
        ProjectDto project = projectApplicationService.getProjectByRef(ref);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(project);
    }
}
```

### Avoid Wildcard Imports

```java
// Good
import com.example.api.generated.model.ProjectDto;
import com.example.api.generated.model.CreateProjectRequestDto;

// Bad
import com.example.api.generated.model.*;
```

## Mapper Pattern

Mappers convert between domain entities and DTOs:

```java
@Component
public class ProjectMapper {

    public ProjectDto toDto(Project domain) {
        ProjectDto dto = new ProjectDto();
        dto.setProjectId(domain.getProjectId());
        dto.setTitle(domain.getTitle());
        dto.setSequenceNumber(domain.getSequenceNumber());
        return dto;
    }

    public Project toDomain(CreateProjectRequestDto dto) {
        return new Project(dto.getTitle(), 0); // sequence number set later
    }
}
```

## Reference Resolution Pattern

Since entities are looked up by `ref` (external identifier), provide a resolver:

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class RefResolver {
    private final ProjectRepository projectRepository;

    public Project resolve(String ref) {
        return projectRepository.findByRef(ref)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new EntityNotFoundException("Project", ref));
    }
}
```

## Exception Handling

### Custom Exceptions

```java
public class EntityNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public EntityNotFoundException(String entityType, String reference) {
        super(entityType + " not found: " + reference);
    }
}
```

### Global Exception Handler

```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(EntityNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponseDto> handleNotFound(EntityNotFoundException ex) {
        ErrorResponseDto error = new ErrorResponseDto();
        error.setCode("NOT_FOUND");
        error.setMessage(ex.getMessage());
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(error);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponseDto> handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
        ErrorResponseDto error = new ErrorResponseDto();
        error.setCode("VALIDATION_ERROR");
        error.setMessage("Validation failed");
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body(error);
    }
}
```

## Code Style

### Avoid Wildcard Imports
Always use explicit imports.

### Use Modern Switch Expressions

```java
private SequenceStatus toApiStatus(SequenceStatus domain) {
    return switch (domain) {
        case ACTIVE -> SequenceStatusDto.ACTIVE;
        case INACTIVE -> SequenceStatusDto.INACTIVE;
    };
}
```

